  "decision_summary": "The query is a small, relatively lipophilic peptidomimetic with a leucine side chain and a cyano-cyclopropyl amide. The strongest transferable evidence is from Excitin-1, which shares the leucine-amide scaffold and enters the brain, and from leucine itself, which crosses the BBB rapidly. Additional support comes from fluorinated amide CNS penetrants. No contradictory evidence was identified. Overall, the molecule is predicted to have meaningful CNS access.",
